  "question": {
    "text": "If non-zero numbers $a, b, c$ are in H.P., then the straight line $\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}+\\frac{1}{c}=0$ always passes through a fixed point. That point is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4HYIR",
      "text": "\n$(-1,2)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NawgO",
      "text": "\n$(-1,-2)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CG3Gv",
      "text": "\n$(1,-2)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "yrblS",
      "text": "\n$\\left(1,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "a, b, c are in H.P.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{b}-\\frac{1}{a}-\\frac{1}{c}=0 \\\\\n& \\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}+\\frac{1}{c}=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{x}{-1} \\quad-\\frac{1}{-1} \\quad \\therefore x=1, y=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
